  "summary": "The quotient and square identities, reduction formulae and co-functions, negative angles, proving identities, and finding the general solution of trigonometric equations.",
  "notes": [
    { "type": "heading", "text": "Identities" },
    { "type": "formula", "latex": "\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} \\qquad \\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1", "caption": "The quotient identity and the square identity" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "text": "The square identity can be rearranged: $\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta$ and $\\cos^2\\theta = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta$." },
    { "type": "example", "title": "Worked example 1: proving an identity", "problem": "Prove that $\\dfrac{1 - \\cos^2 x}{\\sin x \\cos x} = \\tan x$", "steps": [
      "LHS $= \\dfrac{\\sin^2 x}{\\sin x \\cos x}$ (square identity)",
      "$= \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\tan x =$ RHS (quotient identity)"
    ], "answer": "LHS = RHS" },
    { "type": "callout", "label": "Exam tip", "text": "Work on one side at a time (usually the more complicated one). Change $\\tan$ into $\\dfrac{\\sin}{\\cos}$, look for $\\sin^2 + \\cos^2$, and find common denominators. Never move terms across the equals sign in a proof." },
    { "type": "heading", "text": "Reduction formulae" },
    { "type": "table", "caption": "Use the CAST diagram to choose the sign", "headers": ["Angle", "$\\sin$", "$\\cos$", "$\\tan$"], "rows": [
      ["$180^\\circ - \\theta$ (Q2)", "$\\sin\\theta$", "$-\\cos\\theta$", "$-\\tan\\theta$"],
      ["$180^\\circ + \\theta$ (Q3)", "$-\\sin\\theta$", "$-\\cos\\theta$", "$\\tan\\theta$"],
      ["$360^\\circ - \\theta$ (Q4)", "$-\\sin\\theta$", "$\\cos\\theta$", "$-\\tan\\theta$"],
      ["$-\\theta$", "$-\\sin\\theta$", "$\\cos\\theta$", "$-\\tan\\theta$"],
      ["$360^\\circ + \\theta$", "$\\sin\\theta$", "$\\cos\\theta$", "$\\tan\\theta$"]
    ] },
    { "type": "formula", "latex": "\\sin(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\cos\\theta \\qquad \\cos(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\sin\\theta", "caption": "Co-functions (also $\\sin(90^\\circ + \\theta) = \\cos\\theta$ and $\\cos(90^\\circ + \\theta) = -\\sin\\theta$)" },
    { "type": "example", "title": "Worked example 2", "problem": "Simplify without a calculator: $\\dfrac{\\sin(180^\\circ + x)\\cos(90^\\circ - x)}{\\sin^2(-x)}$", "steps": [
      "$\\sin(180^\\circ + x) = -\\sin x$; $\\cos(90^\\circ - x) = \\sin x$; $\\sin^2(-x) = (-\\sin x)^2 = \\sin^2 x$",
      "$= \\dfrac{-\\sin x \\cdot \\sin x}{\\sin^2 x} = -1$"
    ], "answer": "$-1$" },
    { "type": "example", "title": "Worked example 3: special angles", "problem": "Evaluate without a calculator: $\\cos 300^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 225^\\circ$", "steps": ["$\\cos 300^\\circ = \\cos(360^\\circ - 60^\\circ) = \\cos 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2}$", "$\\tan 225^\\circ = \\tan(180^\\circ + 45^\\circ) = \\tan 45^\\circ = 1$", "Product $= \\frac{1}{2}$"], "answer": "$\\frac{1}{2}$" },
    { "type": "heading", "text": "General solutions" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "text": "Because trigonometric functions repeat, an equation such as $\\sin\\theta = 0{,}5$ has infinitely many solutions. The **general solution** describes all of them, with $k \\in \\mathbb{Z}$." },
    { "type": "table", "headers": ["Equation", "General solution"], "rows": [
      ["$\\sin\\theta = x$", "$\\theta = \\text{ref} + k \\cdot 360^\\circ$ or $\\theta = (180^\\circ - \\text{ref}) + k \\cdot 360^\\circ$"],
      ["$\\cos\\theta = x$", "$\\theta = \\pm\\text{ref} + k \\cdot 360^\\circ$"],
      ["$\\tan\\theta = x$", "$\\theta = \\text{ref} + k \\cdot 180^\\circ$"]
    ] },
    { "type": "example", "title": "Worked example 4", "problem": "Find the general solution of $2\\cos(2x) = -1$, and the solutions in $[0^\\circ; 180^\\circ]$.", "steps": [
